+# S5-CLM-00003488 frontier
+
+The frozen proposition is the `Claim` polarity
+
+`∀ k : ℕ, 0 < k → Set.Infinite {p : ℕ | IsSecondKindChainOfLength p k}`.
+
+The source record calls this the second-kind Cunningham-chain infinitude
+conjecture and marks it research-open. The target-local statement file
+preserves the source recurrence and predicate and proves only definitional
+transport; it does not manufacture a global theorem.
+
+## Typed frontier
+
+| node | kind | exact obligation | current evidence | cut |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `STMT-EXACT-001` | statement binding | elaborate the exact universal proposition | `Statement.lean`, `source_to_target` | none for transport |
+| `CASE-SECOND-001` | finite consequence | `IsSecondKindChainOfLength 7 2` | compiled in `Proof.lean` | does not imply infinitude |
+| `EXP-BOUNDED-001` | exploration | enumerate `p ≤ 10000`, lengths 1–8 | `attempt-001.json` | finite-to-infinite cut |
+| `RES-ROOT-OPEN` | exact root | prove `Claim` or prove `Not Claim` | absent by design | mapping, human, machine, readable |
+
+The four cuts are independent. The finite enumerator mirrors the pinned
+recurrence only inside its declared finite boundary; it cannot be promoted to
+a theorem about all natural starting primes.
+
+## Proof route candidates
+
+1. Establish a uniform construction of infinitely many starts for each positive
+   exact length, likely via the arithmetic of the recurrence `q ↦ 2q - 1`.
+2. Prove a suitable prime-pattern or covering argument without replacing the
+   exact-length predicate by a bounded surrogate.
+3. Translate that argument to the exact Lean definitions with no fixed search
+   bound and no source-body oracle.
+
+## Refutation route candidates
+
+1. Exhibit a positive `k` for which the set of starts is finite.
+2. Prove that finiteness in Lean and derive the exact `Not Claim` polarity.
+3. Treat a finite search failure only as evidence, never as a finiteness proof.
+
+No route is closed in this handoff. The package is therefore an accepted
+exploration handoff, not a resolution or release acceptance.
