+# Human resolution
+
+## Exact polarity
+
+The frozen source proposition is a `Claim`, not a negated claim:
+
+```text
+∀ k : ℕ, 0 < k → Set.Infinite {p : ℕ | IsSecondKindChainOfLength p k}.
+```
+
+The source file describes this as a conjecture and leaves its body unresolved.
+The target package preserves that status. It does not treat the source body, a
+docstring, a finite computation, or a literature citation as a proof term.
+
+## What was checked
+
+The exact recurrence is `q ↦ 2q - 1`, with natural-number subtraction as in
+the source. A deterministic local enumeration for `p ≤ 10000` found exact
+starts for lengths 1 through 5 (counts 1040, 145, 37, 5, and 2), and no starts
+for lengths 6 through 8 in that finite bound. These observations are
+compatible with the conjecture and also compatible with a finite exceptional
+set. They therefore establish neither `Claim` nor `Not Claim`.
+
+The checked source test `IsSecondKindChainOfLength 7 2` is a finite sanity
+case only. A proof would need a uniform construction or theorem yielding
+infinitely many starts for every positive `k`; a refutation would need one
+positive `k` together with a proof that its set of starts is finite. Neither
+object was found or assumed in this run.
+
+## Resolution
+
+No complete human proof or refutation exists in the target-local evidence.
+The outcome is `open`, and the worker cannot advance RELEASE to `x`. A future
+attempt must append new evidence under this same TARGET identity and bind the
+same statement fingerprint before any terminal outcome is considered.
